# Week 8 Learning Journal – Learning Experiment and Presentation Rehearsal

**Date:** 25 July 2026

## Overview

This week focused on conducting a learning experiment and preparing for our group project presentation. I also continued communicating with my teammates through Discord while working on our project tasks and discussing our progress.

## Learning Experiment

### Hypothesis

I believe that practising PHP by writing and testing small pieces of code step by step is more effective than only reading lecture slides or watching videos.

### Experiment

To test this idea, I divided my study into two different approaches.

- **Method 1:** I spent 30 minutes reading the lecture slides and reviewing PHP syntax without writing any code.
- **Method 2:** I spent 30 minutes creating PHP files, running the code in my local environment, fixing errors, and testing different PHP features such as `echo`, `if/else`, loops, functions and `include`.

After each session, I wrote down how much I remembered and whether I could complete similar coding tasks without looking at the notes.

### Results

The practical coding session was much more effective. I understood PHP concepts more clearly because I could immediately see the results in the browser and identify mistakes while coding. Reading the slides helped me understand the theory, but writing and testing code improved my confidence and problem-solving skills.

### Conclusion

The experiment supported my hypothesis. Practising by writing and testing PHP code helped me learn faster than reading theory alone. I will continue using this approach when learning new programming topics.

